From knutin at urtete.com  Sun Mar  9 18:23:40 2008
From: knutin at urtete.com (Knut Ivar Nesheim)
Date: Sun, 09 Mar 2008 19:23:40 +0100
Subject: [Rpy] Empty values
Message-ID: <642B233A-BD2B-4387-87EE-263FEB786C7A@urtete.com>

Hi!

I'm wondering how one would go about plotting nothing.

Lets say I have a dataset with values for each day of the month. Now,  
this is fine until the day where there's no data, ie. Sunday. One  
could simply ignore the days without any data, but that is not desired  
in this case.

Let's say I have a list of data, [10.5, 11.3, 10.2, None, 10.7] and  
I'm using r.plot(data, type = "l"), None will be treated as 0.0  
instead of just empty. Same thing if I use type = "o" or whatever.

I want the line just to stop where there's no data and then continue  
again where I have some data. How would I do that?

Regards,
Knut Ivar Nesheim



